HST Office on Linux: own launcher ids, window classes and app ids, never LibreOffice's.

With a distribution LibreOffice installed beside HST:
- both used the window class (X11 WM_CLASS) and Wayland app_id libreoffice-<module> and HST's
  launchers declared StartupWMClass=libreoffice-*, so the desktop shell grouped HST windows under
  LibreOffice's launcher and icon, and LibreOffice's under HST's;
- update-desktop-database lists the handlers of a MIME type sorted by launcher id, and without a
  configured default GLib (GNOME, Cinnamon, Xfce) and xdg-mime open a file with the first one:
  hst-office1.0-writer.desktop sorted before libreoffice-writer.desktop, so installing HST made it
  the default application for ODF and OOXML files in place of LibreOffice.
Now the launchers and application icons are vn.hasontech.hstoffice-<module> (DESKTOPID.hst_office,
the AppStream component id), which sorts after every LibreOffice id; the window class, the Wayland
app_id and the window icon are that same id (include/hst_desktop_id.h) and each launcher's
StartupWMClass. KDE orders handlers by InitialPreference: HST's is 4, one below LibreOffice's 5.
The start center no longer claims LibreOffice's own URL schemes (vnd.libreoffice.cmis/command,
vnd.sun.star.webdav/webdavs); the Microsoft Office ms-* schemes and .oxt stay.
HST stays under Open With and is the default where no other suite is installed. The commands,
install root (/opt/hst-office1.0) and package names are unchanged; macOS and Windows keep their
own identifiers.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0); include/hst_desktop_id.h
is new and under MPL-2.0 like the files that use it.

--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/hst_desktop_id.h
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+/* -*- Mode: C++; tab-width: 4; indent-tabs-mode: nil; c-basic-offset: 4; fill-column: 100 -*- */
+/*
+ * This Source Code Form is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public
+ * License, v. 2.0. If a copy of the MPL was not distributed with this
+ * file, You can obtain one at http://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.
+ */
+
+#pragma once
+
+// HST Office on Linux: the launchers are /usr/share/applications/<id>-<module>.desktop and the
+// application icons <id>-<module>, with <id> = DESKTOPID.hst_office of sysui/productlist.mk. The
+// window class (X11 WM_CLASS), the Wayland app_id and the window icon use the same names, so a
+// desktop shell maps every HST window to its own launcher, never to libreoffice-<module>.desktop
+// of a LibreOffice installed beside HST. The reverse-DNS id also sorts after every LibreOffice
+// launcher id, so the MIME cache does not put HST first (see sysui/productlist.mk).
+#define HST_DESKTOP_ID_PREFIX "vn.hasontech.hstoffice"
+
+/* vim:set shiftwidth=4 softtabstop=4 expandtab cinoptions=b1,g0,N-s cinkeys+=0=break: */
--- a/vcl/source/app/IconHelper.cxx
+++ b/vcl/source/app/IconHelper.cxx
@@ -12,24 +12,38 @@
 
 #include <vcl/bitmaps.hlst>
 
+#if defined UNX && !defined MACOSX
+#include <hst_desktop_id.h>
+#endif
+
+// Window icon and Wayland app_id of a module: the id of its launcher (.desktop file).
+static OUString lcl_appIconName(const char* pModule)
+{
+#if defined UNX && !defined MACOSX
+    return OUString::createFromAscii(HST_DESKTOP_ID_PREFIX "-") + OUString::createFromAscii(pModule);
+#else
+    return u"libreoffice-"_ustr + OUString::createFromAscii(pModule);
+#endif
+}
+
 OUString IconHelper::GetAppIconName(sal_uInt16 nIcon)
 {
     switch (nIcon)
     {
         case SV_ICON_ID_TEXT:
-            return u"libreoffice-writer"_ustr;
+            return lcl_appIconName("writer");
         case SV_ICON_ID_SPREADSHEET:
-            return u"libreoffice-calc"_ustr;
+            return lcl_appIconName("calc");
         case SV_ICON_ID_DRAWING:
-            return u"libreoffice-draw"_ustr;
+            return lcl_appIconName("draw");
         case SV_ICON_ID_PRESENTATION:
-            return u"libreoffice-impress"_ustr;
+            return lcl_appIconName("impress");
         case SV_ICON_ID_DATABASE:
-            return u"libreoffice-base"_ustr;
+            return lcl_appIconName("base");
         case SV_ICON_ID_FORMULA:
-            return u"libreoffice-math"_ustr;
+            return lcl_appIconName("math");
         default:
-            return u"libreoffice-startcenter"_ustr;
+            return lcl_appIconName("startcenter");
     }
 }
 
